{"ref":"BDB, קָרָה⁴","hw":"קָרָה⁴","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">קָרָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f.</strong> id.;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּיוֹם ק׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 3:17\" href=\"/Nahum.3.17\">Na 3:17</a> <em>a day of coldness</em>, cold day, so <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 25:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.25.20\">Pr 25:20</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ק׳</span> alone, <em>cold</em> of night <a data-ref=\"Job 24:7\" href=\"/Job.24.7\">Jb 24:7</a>; in gen., due to winds <a data-ref=\"Job 37:9\" href=\"/Job.37.9\">37:9</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">מִמְּזָרִים</span> v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, זָרָה\" href=\"/BDB,_זָרָה\", dir=\"rtl\">זרה</a> <strong>Pi.</strong>; yet Voigt Bu, attractively, <span dir=\"rtl\">מִמְּזָוִים</span> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 144:13\" href=\"/Psalms.144.13\">ψ 144:13</a>) <em>out of storehouses</em> [‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">חֶדֶר</span>]); <span dir=\"rtl\">לִפְנֵי קָרָתוֹ מִי יַעֲמֹד</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 147:17\" href=\"/Psalms.147.17\">ψ 147:17</a>, + pl. <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 14:6\" href=\"/Zechariah.14.6\">Zc 14:6</a> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">וְקָרוֹת</span>, v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, יָקָר\" href=\"/BDB,_יָקָר\", dir=\"rtl\">יָקָר</a>).","next":"BDB, מְקֵרָה²","prev":"BDB, קֹר"}